    {
      "candidateId": "mv.environment.randomization-tools.63a16724",
      "proposedType": "environment",
      "proposedName": "Randomization Tools",
      "summary": "Create a system for GMs to generate courses quickly using roll tables or card decks. a. Roll Tables 1.Course Length (1d6): •1-2: Short (3-5 sections). •3-4: Medium (6-10 sections). •5-6: Long (11+ sections). 2.Terrain (1d8): •1: Straightaway. •2: Curve. •3: Incline. •4: Decline. •5: Interdimensional Rift. •6: Water Hazard. •7: Lava Field. •8: Dense Urban Area. 3.Hazards (1d10): •1: None. •2-3: Static hazard (e.g., cliffs). •4-5: Dynamic hazard (e.g., falling rocks). •6-7: Opponent or creature encounter. •8: Weather condition (e.g., blizzard). •9: Vehicle malfunction area (requires repairs). •10: Combined hazards (GMʼs choice). 4.Boost Opportunities (1d4): •1: Speed booster. •2: Energy recharge zone. •3: Shortcut path. •4: No boost opportunities. b. Card Decks Design cards with pre-written challenges, hazards, and features. GMs draw a set number of cards to build the course, adding flexibility and replayability.",
      "source": {
