      "proposedType": "environment",
      "proposedName": "The Broken Shell and the Floating Edge",
      "summary": "Dionasiaʼs surface is a puzzle of dislocated landmasses, shattered crustal plates, and sky-facing chasms. Its geography is not shaped by tectonics or erosion, but by the slow drift of Gravity Wells, the lingering scars of the Great Fracturing, and the upward-pulling void that threatens to reclaim everything. Most of Dionasia's inhabited terrain exists on the underside of cliffs, ridgelines, or mountaintops suspended over vast abyssal skies. Terrain is defined by height, gravitational alignment, proximity to Gravity Wells, and accessibility by skybeast or cable transit.",
